Perform a security review of this Express/TypeScript endpoint. List every vulnerability you find ranked by severity, explain how each would be exploited, and provide a hardened rewrite.

import express from 'express';
import jwt from 'jsonwebtoken';
import { db } from './db';
import fs from 'fs';

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

app.get('/api/invoice', (req, res) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  const user: any = jwt.decode(token as string);
  const q = `SELECT * FROM invoices WHERE owner = '${user.id}' AND number = '${req.query.number}'`;
  db.query(q, (err: any, rows: any[]) => {
    if (err) return res.status(500).send(err.stack);
    const file = './pdfs/' + rows[0].file;
    res.type('pdf').send(fs.readFileSync(file));
  });
});

app.listen(3000);

A C# endpoint using EF Core takes 12 seconds to return 500 orders. Diagnose the likely performance problems in the code below and rewrite it. Quantify the expected query count before and after, and explain what you would measure to confirm.

public async Task<List<OrderDto>> GetOrders(int customerId)
{
    var orders = _db.Orders.ToList().Where(o => o.CustomerId == customerId).ToList();
    var result = new List<OrderDto>();
    foreach (var o in orders)
    {
        var lines = _db.OrderLines.Where(l => l.OrderId == o.Id).ToList();
        var product = _db.Products.First(p => p.Id == lines[0].ProductId);
        string summary = "";
        foreach (var l in lines)
            summary += l.Quantity + "x " + _db.Products.First(p => p.Id == l.ProductId).Name + ", ";
        result.Add(new OrderDto { Id = o.Id, Summary = summary, Main = product.Name });
    }
    return result;
}

This Java bank transfer code occasionally deadlocks in production. Explain precisely how, fix it with a safe lock-ordering scheme that also handles transferring to the same account and accounts with equal hash codes, and write a test that reliably demonstrates the original deadlock using timeouts.

class Account {
    final long id;
    long balance;
    Account(long id, long balance) { this.id = id; this.balance = balance; }
}

class Bank {
    void transfer(Account from, Account to, long amount) {
        synchronized (from) {
            synchronized (to) {
                if (from.balance < amount) throw new IllegalStateException("insufficient");
                from.balance -= amount;
                to.balance += amount;
            }
        }
    }
}
